==Features==
===Insurance===
All insured items left in a raid by players will not be returned. Upon death, insurance [[Traders]] will send the usual in-game mail about dispatching people to recover the items, but when the insurance timer runs out they will explain that their people don't go to the location, didn't find it or died in the process.

[[File:The Labyrinth insurance message.png]]

===Spawn chambers===
Each of the 5 spawns has its entry to the rest of the location blocked by a hazard/trap, which needs to be resolved to not die.

=====Chamber 1 - Toxic pool=====
[[File:The Labyrinth Chamber 1 - Toxic pool.png|thumb|right|200px|Toxic pool]]
1. Find [[Key 01]]

2. Unlock the door in the left side room

3. Press the button on the wall

=====Chamber 2 - Steam hazard=====
[[File:The Labyrinth Chamber 2 - Steam hazard.png|thumb|right|200px|Steam hazard]]
1. Find [[Key 02]]

2. Unlock the red door

3. Find the [[Valve handwheel]] on the 2nd floor

4. Apply the handwheel to the pipe next to the yellow door on the 1st floor

=====Chamber 3 - Fire hazard=====
[[File:The Labyrinth Chamber 3 - Fire hazard.png|thumb|right|200px|Fire hazard]]
1. Find [[Key 03]]

2. Unlock the far door

3. Find the [[BBQ-S43 gas torch]]

4. Apply the gas torch to the door at the start

5. Press the button at the electrical cabinet

=====Chamber 4 - Shotgun trap=====
[[File:The Labyrinth Chamber 4 - Shotgun trap.png|thumb|right|200px|Shotgun trap]]
1. Find [[Key 04]]

2. Unlock the 2nd door

3. Crawl into the connected room

4. Pull the lever to the left of the door

5. Breach the door

=====Chamber 5 - Toxic puddle=====
[[File:The Labyrinth Chamber 5 - Toxic puddle.png|thumb|right|200px|Toxic puddle]]
1. Find the [[BBQ-S43 gas torch]]

2. Apply the gas torch to the round door in the left side room

3. Pull the lever on the wall

===Traps===
=====Tripwires=====
The [[tripwire]]s placed by [[Shadow of Tagilla]] on raid start have set locations. They automatically disarm after 20 minutes and don't get set off by Shadow of Tagilla.

=====Poisoned barbed wire=====
The barbed wire has set locations, but it is random in which it appears every raid. Upon contact, there is a chance to get inflicted with the [[File:Intoxication.png|46px|Unknown toxin]] effect, which deals gradual damage over time (140 HP/minute). It can be treated with an [[xTG-12 antidote injector|xTG-12]] or [[Perfotoran (Blue Blood) stimulant injector|Perfotoran]] injector.
<li style="display: inline-block;"><gallery widths="300" heights="169" mode="packed">
File:The Labyrinth Barbed Wire.png
</gallery></li>

=====Spike pits=====
The pits are always present in set locations, but randomly open or closed every raid.
<li style="display: inline-block;"><gallery widths="300" heights="169" mode="packed">
File:The Labyrinth Spike Pit Closed.png|Closed spike pit
File:The Labyrinth Spike Pit Open.png|Open spike pit
</gallery></li>

===Alarm===
Whenever a player goes near the center of the labyrinth, an alarm sounds. It can be deactivated with multiple buttons spread across the location.

[[File:TheLabyrinthAlarm.wav|282px]]
